### 1. Login: obtiene el token
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "admin", "password": "Interseguro2026"}

### 2. QR con token (usa el token del login automáticamente)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/qr
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{"matrix": [[12, -51, 4], [6, 167, -68], [-4, 24, -41]]}

### 3. QR sin token: debe dar 401
POST http://localhost:8080/api/qr
Content-Type: application/json

{"matrix": [[12, -51, 4], [6, 167, -68], [-4, 24, -41]]}

### 4. Login con contraseña incorrecta: debe dar 401
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "admin", "password": "incorrecta"}

### 5. Error de validación (con token)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/qr
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{"matrix": [[1, 2], [3]]}